> > would seem to be required.

a conscious being, R Bryner wrote:
> Only a verifiable identity, which could be an md5 hash of a public key
> signature of a vote code and the message id, or even less to save space. 

I would think it is useful to think of "voting" in two contexts...

SYSTEM 1: One is for providing feedback to a system in which the
information resulting from the feedback is processed algorithmically
and is used to find other posts you might like.

SYSTEM 2: The other is for voting in which the votes are to be made
public and can be used in several ways.

1) a user can see how he/she is "doing"; peer review...

2) users can enter commands to get posts specifically highly rated by
   specific users (::include posts ranked +4 <minsky@mit.edu> )

In terms of the filtering Ray will be building for the new software we
are looking at building the first system rather than the second, but
the data could be used by both....

If we just used it for system 1 or if we used it for both, which would
lead to a system were fewer people defected by voting (we call it
ranking) incorrectly.

My feeling is system 1 should be used alone... people using the system
will get results from it based 100% of how good they rank messages...
using the results in other ways might cause them to defect...


